notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. The gyro moves the mouse, which the game reads beside the pad.
{start} (Escape) opens the game's menu and backs out of every screen in it.
{south} uses (buttons, ladders, pick-ups), {east} jumps, {west} reloads and {north} is the flashlight. {lt} is the right mouse button, the alternate fire of the weapons that have one (the .357's scope, the MP5 grenade launcher, the crossbow's zoom).
A light push of the left stick {ls} walks slowly (Shift); a full push runs. {l3} toggles crouch, and it stays on until you click it again.
{lb} and {rb} step to the previous and next weapon (mouse wheel). {r3} selects the crowbar (slot 1), {left} jumps back to the last weapon and {up} opens a ring of the weapon slots, aimed with the right stick {rs}; pressing a slot again steps through the weapons in it.
Quick save is a double tap of {start} (F6), and quick load a long press of {start} (F7). {down} sprays your logo (T) and {right} opens the developer console (~), if you turned it on in the game's options.
The keys are the game's defaults. If you changed them in Options → Controls, change them here too. Half-Life: Source and the expansions (Opposing Force, Blue Shift) use the same keys.
{guide} still works over the game: {guide} + {west} opens the on-screen keyboard and {guide} + {lb} the media controls.
If the game stops answering the pad, check that Steam Input or another remapper isn't also running for it.'''

